      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As someone with fine-motor issues who would like to be able to use the new AudioLink panel, I would love to see this change implemented.\n\nThe grab distance of the 2nd handle prevents me from manipulating the UI unless I hold it at nearly arms length. At that distance, the natural shaking of my hands combined with the imprecision of the controllers makes it quite a painful experience! Literally and metaphorically.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-12-01T16:14:40.491Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, there are scenarios where users ability to interact with objects at a distance is interfered with by other nearby objects. A notable example is in activities like playing cards, where the need to pick up cards on the table exists, but the proximity of the cards in front of the user can be obstructive.\n\nTo address this, I propose separating the laser and hover proximity values. This would allow users to fine-tune the distance at which they can grab objects with the two methods, providing a more tailored and immersive experience. By having separate proximity settings, users could seamlessly engage with objects both near and far, eliminating potential obstructions and enhancing the overall usability of VRChat.",
